  "mode": "baked",
  "note": "The face is painted on the paper like ink: the eyes are shallow glossy lenses (lo_eyes) with the brown iris, its amber lower half, the pupil and two catchlights baked into the body atlas; the ink outlines, the brows, the small smile, the blush and the closed lids' lash lines are baked into the body. No face sheet and no morphs: expressions in clips' `faces` are hints only; the mouth never opens. Blinking scales the blink bones (play `blink` over any clip): each lens squashes onto the painted lash line and sinks under the paper. The inner light is the glow map (ORM alpha, in the paper's own colour; Beacon's tinted #FFB85C): modest on the paper and the paddles, hot over the flame inside the opening; socket_core sits at the flame (the pulse strike's beam).",
